course: history
lesson: 50
title: Today's Ukraine and Danylo's exaggerations
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Danylo loves Ukraine so much that his stories grow in the telling, like a fish that gets bigger each time a fisherman describes it; this lesson checks his favourite claims one by one, and sometimes he is completely right.
explain: Ukraine is the largest country lying wholly in Europe, Russia being bigger only if you count its Asian land; a Kyiv-born engineer, Igor Sikorsky, made the helicopter practical; and «Carol of the Bells», sung in American films every Christmas, is the Ukrainian song «Shchedryk».
explain: But there was no world contest that crowned Ukrainian «the most melodious language», the kerosene lamp was made in Lviv by a Polish pharmacist, decorated eggs exist in many cultures, and Ukraine has won Eurovision three times, not «always».
explain: Ukrainian is the state language, yet many families spoke Russian at home for historical reasons; Danylo's parents switched to Ukrainian in 2022, and the teacher said language choice is personal and changing.
explain: The wise lesson: agree on definitions first, love your country without inventing prizes or firsts, and say thank you when a pupil teaches you something true.
fact: Ukraine, about 603,000 square kilometres, is the largest country entirely in Europe; Russia is larger, and even its European part alone is bigger than Ukraine.
fact: Many people find Ukrainian melodious, but the story that it won a world contest as the second most melodious language after Italian has no real source.
fact: Igor Sikorsky, born in Kyiv in 1889, built the first practical mass-produced helicopters, the VS-300 and R-4, in the USA; others in France and elsewhere built earlier rotorcraft.
fact: In 1853 Ignacy Łukasiewicz, a Polish pharmacist, and Jan Zeh made a kerosene lamp in Lviv, then in the Austrian Empire, and it lit a hospital operation.
fact: Serhii Korolev, chief designer of the Soviet space programme, was born in Zhytomyr; the Yuzhmash plant in Dnipro built many Soviet rockets; Yuri Kondratiuk from Poltava calculated the lunar orbit route later used by NASA's Apollo missions.
fact: In 2022 UNESCO, the United Nations body for culture, inscribed the culture of Ukrainian borscht cooking as heritage in need of urgent safeguarding; borscht is also cooked in Poland, Lithuania, Russia and elsewhere.
fact: The vyshyvanka is the embroidered shirt, with regional patterns and colours; Vyshyvanka Day is in May, and some motifs have traditional meanings, while many are decoration and local style.
fact: Pysanky are eggs decorated by drawing with wax and dipping in dyes, an old tradition; the wax keeps the dye off the lines it covers; Kolomyia has a pysanka museum shaped like a giant egg, and decorated eggs exist in many cultures.
fact: «Carol of the Bells» is based on «Shchedryk», a Ukrainian New Year song arranged by Mykola Leontovych; a Ukrainian choir sang it in New York in 1922, and Peter Wilhousky later wrote the English words.
fact: Ukrainian is the state language; for historical reasons many Ukrainians, especially in big cities and the east, spoke Russian at home, and since 2014, and more since 2022, many have switched to Ukrainian.
fact: Ukraine won Eurovision in 2004 (Ruslana), 2016 (Jamala with «1944») and 2022 (Kalush Orchestra).
fact: Ukraine applied to join the EU in February 2022, became a candidate in June 2022, and accession talks (talks about joining) formally opened in June 2024; it is a candidate, not yet a member.
exercise: Which is the largest country lying entirely in Europe? | Ukraine | Mainland France | Russia, the giant | Unified Germany
exercise: About how big is Ukraine? | About 603,000 square kilometres | About 6,000 square kilometres | About 6 million square kilometres | About 60 square kilometres
exercise: Is there a real world contest that named Ukrainian the most melodious language? | No, the story has no real source | Yes, held in Paris in 1934 | Yes, held every year by UNESCO | Yes, won by Ukrainian ahead of Italian
exercise: Where was Igor Sikorsky born? | Kyiv | Paris | New York | Lviv in Galicia
exercise: Where did Sikorsky build his helicopters? | In the USA | In Kyiv, his home city | In Sweden, near Stockholm | In Japan, for the army
exercise: Who made the kerosene lamp in Lviv in 1853? | Ignacy Łukasiewicz, a Polish pharmacist, with Jan Zeh | Taras Shevchenko | Igor Sikorsky, before he moved to America to build aircraft | Bohdan Khmelnytsky
exercise: Where was Serhii Korolev, the Soviet chief rocket designer, born? | Zhytomyr | Moscow in Russia | Odesa on the Black Sea | Lviv in Galicia
exercise: What did Yuri Kondratiuk calculate? | A route to the Moon via lunar orbit | The exact length of the river Dnipro from source to sea | The first hryvnia exchange rate | The height of the Carpathians
exercise: What did UNESCO inscribe in 2022? | The culture of Ukrainian borscht cooking | A ban on cooking borscht anywhere outside Ukraine | The recipe owned by one cook | Borscht as a Russian dish only
exercise: How can you often tell which region a vyshyvanka comes from? | By its patterns and colours | By its smell | By the price written on the label | By the size of its buttons
exercise: How is wax used to make a pysanka? | It covers parts of the egg so dye does not colour them | It glues the cracked shell back together so it does not leak | It makes the egg bounce | It is eaten with the egg
exercise: What was the original Ukrainian song behind «Carol of the Bells»? | «Shchedryk» | Shevchenko's «Zapovit» | Jamala's «1944» | Kalush's «Stefania»
exercise: Who arranged «Shchedryk»? | Mykola Leontovych | Ivan Franko | Ruslana | Peter the Great
exercise: Why did many Ukrainians switch to Ukrainian after 2022? | As a personal choice after the full-scale invasion | Because Russian was forgotten overnight by everyone in the country | Because Eurovision required it | Because it was the only language taught in 1991
exercise: How many times has Ukraine won Eurovision? | Three times | Every single year | Only once, in 2004 | Never, not even once
exercise: Which Ukrainian Eurovision song was about history? | Jamala's «1944» | Ruslana's «Wild Dances» | Kalush Orchestra's «Stefania» | «Carol of the Bells»
exercise: What is Ukraine's status in the EU today? | A candidate in accession talks | A full member since 2004 | A founding member | Not a candidate at all
test: Danylo says Ukraine's the biggest country in Europe, teacher says Russia's bigger. Who's right? | Both, depending on the definition: Ukraine is the largest wholly in Europe | Only Danylo | Only the teacher | Neither, France is bigger than both of them once you add in all its overseas lands
test: «ukrainian won 2nd place for most beautiful language, after italian, look it up». What do you find? | No real contest exists; it's a popular myth | The official certificate from 1934 | A UN medal ceremony | A ranking by the Pope
test: Danylo says Ukrainians invented the helicopter. What's the exact way to say it? | A Kyiv-born engineer made the helicopter practical, working in America | Ukrainians invented every flying machine, from the balloon to the jet plane | Sikorsky never built anything | The helicopter was invented in Kyiv in 1500
test: Danylo says Ukrainians invented the kerosene lamp; teacher says the inventor was Polish. Best answer? | Both: invented in Lviv, now Ukrainian, by a Polish pharmacist | Only Danylo is right | Only the teacher is right, because Lviv doesn't count as Ukraine | It was invented in Sweden
test: Danylo says Ukrainians built all the Soviet rockets. What's fairer? | Ukrainian-born people and factories played a big part among many peoples | Every bolt of every Soviet rocket was made in a factory in Kyiv, Dnipro or Kharkiv | No Ukrainian ever worked on rockets | Rockets were built only in America
test: Danylo says nobody else is allowed to make borscht now. What's true? | UNESCO protects a tradition; anyone may still cook it | Making borscht abroad is a crime | UNESCO banned borscht | Borscht was invented in Italy
test: Danylo says every vyshyvanka pattern is a secret code. What's more exact? | Some motifs have meanings, many are decoration and local style | Every stitch is a secret message that only grandmothers can read | Patterns mean nothing ever | They are copied from computer chips
test: «we painted the first easter eggs in the world». What's the wise reply? | Pysanky are a fine old tradition, but decorated eggs exist in many cultures | Yes, the very first, proven | Ukraine never decorated eggs | Eggs were first painted in Kolomyia, and the rest of the world copied them later
test: Danylo says America's most famous Christmas song is Ukrainian. Teacher's amazed. Who's right? | Danylo: «Carol of the Bells» is based on «Shchedryk» | The teacher: it's an English folk song | Neither: it's French | Nobody knows where it came from
test: Danylo says nobody ever spoke Russian in Ukraine. What's the honest picture? | Many did at home for historical reasons, and many have switched to Ukrainian | Nobody ever did | Everyone speaks only Russian at home, at work and at school, even today in Lviv | Ukrainian is not a state language
test: «Ukraine always wins eurovision bro». Fix it. | It won three times: 2004, 2016 and 2022 | It wins every single year | It never won | It won only in 1991
test: Danylo says Ukraine's already in the EU. What's the exact phrase? | A candidate on the way, with talks opened in 2024 | A member since 1991 | It was refused for ever | It founded the EU
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the territorial extent of Ukraine within Europe? | It is the largest state situated wholly within the European continent | It is the largest state in the world | It is smaller than Belgium | It is exceeded in area within Europe by both France and Spain
exam: Identify the origin of the composition known in English as «Carol of the Bells». | The Ukrainian song «Shchedryk», arranged by Mykola Leontovych | An English folk song of the sixteenth century | A Soviet anthem of nineteen hundred and forty-four | A Eurovision entry of two thousand and four
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the inscription made by UNESCO in two thousand and twenty-two in respect of borscht. | The culture of Ukrainian borscht cooking was inscribed as heritage in need of urgent safeguarding | The preparation of borscht outside Ukraine was prohibited by international law in all member states | Borscht was declared the property of a single family | Borscht was removed from all heritage lists
exam: Ascertain the status of Ukraine in respect of the European Union as at the present time. | It is a candidate state with which accession negotiations have formally opened | It has been a full member since nineteen hundred and ninety-one | It is a founding member of the Union | It has never submitted any application for membership to the Union in Brussels
